            <ArticleTitle>[Disability from low back pain in Spain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>491-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Nonspecific low back pain (LBP) is very common and the economic impact of absenteeism has not been completely established in Spain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIAL AND METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">We have valued LBP and the cost of worker's compensation in Spain with the available information between 1993-1997.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The mean LBP was 55,388 per year (SD 9,230.1). The transitory LBP disability was 21.9 days, with a range between 19.7 and 24.2 days. The total cost of worker's compensation LBP claims was 11,000 million pesetas/year, and the mean cost by worker was 209,666 pesetas/year.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The worker's compensation LBP claims was higher in Spain that in the European Union.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
